## 4. What the gallery is evidence of

It shows that something renders. That is less than it appears to be, and the distinction is worth
stating because a gallery is routinely cited as proof of things it cannot demonstrate.

| It does show | It does not show |
|---|---|
| The component renders in at least one configuration | That it renders correctly in the configurations the gallery omits |
| How it looks in the themes the gallery exercises | How it looks in a theme the gallery does not carry |
| That the current build compiles | That behaviour is unchanged since the last build — unless something compares them |

